{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-b8f4f81328c5959c", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# TTSDS2: Resources and Benchmark for Evaluating Human-Quality Text to Speech Systems\narXiv: 2506.19441\nAuthors: \nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: speech_dataset\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Introduction of TTSDS2, a more robust and improved version of the Text to Speech Distribution Score for evaluating synthetic speech.\n  2. Demonstration that TTSDS2 is the only metric out of 16 compared to achieve a Spearman correlation above 0.50 with subjective scores across all evaluated domains.\n  3. Release of a dataset containing over 11,000 subjective opinion score ratings for evaluating synthetic speech close to real speech.\n  4. Release of an automated pipeline for continually recreating a multilingual test dataset to prevent data contamination.\n  5. Release of a continually updated benchmark for evaluating Text to Speech systems across 14 languages.\n\nTags: Eval/嵌入, Eval/基准", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "a8e80990-9f75-43e6-bbad-9b93e69ee810", "uuid": "b7f669c6-fb63-4bc2-add7-02b9e18a8385", "timestamp": "2026-08-13T08:45:05.909Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# TTSDS2: Resources and Benchmark for Evaluating Human-Quality Text to Speech Systems\narXiv: 2506.19441\nAuthors: \nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: speech_dataset\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Introduction of TTSDS2, a more robust and improved version of the Text to Speech Distribution Score for evaluating synthetic speech.\n  2. Demonstration that TTSDS2 is the only metric out of 16 compared to achieve a Spearman correlation above 0.50 with subjective scores across all evaluated domains.\n  3. Release of a dataset containing over 11,000 subjective opinion score ratings for evaluating synthetic speech close to real speech.\n  4. Release of an automated pipeline for continually recreating a multilingual test dataset to prevent data contamination.\n  5. Release of a continually updated benchmark for evaluating Text to Speech systems across 14 languages.\n\nTags: Eval/嵌入, Eval/基准", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-8237379be819a17c", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# Emotion-Aligned Generation in Diffusion Text to Speech Models via Preference-Guided Optimization\narXiv: 2509.25416\nAuthors: Jiacheng Shi, Hongfei Du, Yangfan He, Y. Alicia Hong, Ye Gao\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We propose EASPO, a stepwise alignment framework that reformulates preference optimization as a local, time-conditioned task, replacing the flawed assumption that all intermediate states on a preferred trajectory are equally valid.\n  2. By aligning win/lose candidates at each denoising step from a shared latent, EASPO enables stepwise-controllable emotion shaping throughout the generation process.\n  3. We introduce EASPM, a time-aware reward model that directly scores emotional expressiveness and prosody on noisy intermediate states, enabling dense, temporally grounded preference learning and on-the-fly scoring.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-NAR-Diffusion, TTS/控制-风格标签, TTS/功能-RL优化", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "a8e80990-9f75-43e6-bbad-9b93e69ee810", "uuid": "3e407ae3-fa67-4a5d-a2f7-0a942cffe7af", "timestamp": "2026-08-13T08:45:06.197Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# Emotion-Aligned Generation in Diffusion Text to Speech Models via Preference-Guided Optimization\narXiv: 2509.25416\nAuthors: Jiacheng Shi, Hongfei Du, Yangfan He, Y. Alicia Hong, Ye Gao\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We propose EASPO, a stepwise alignment framework that reformulates preference optimization as a local, time-conditioned task, replacing the flawed assumption that all intermediate states on a preferred trajectory are equally valid.\n  2. By aligning win/lose candidates at each denoising step from a shared latent, EASPO enables stepwise-controllable emotion shaping throughout the generation process.\n  3. We introduce EASPM, a time-aware reward model that directly scores emotional expressiveness and prosody on noisy intermediate states, enabling dense, temporally grounded preference learning and on-the-fly scoring.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-NAR-Diffusion, TTS/控制-风格标签, TTS/功能-RL优化", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-b0f1a6ba2a3507c9", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# Aliasing-Free Neural Audio Synthesis\narXiv: 2512.20211\nAuthors: Yicheng Gu, Junan Zhang, Chaoren Wang, Jerry Li, Zhizheng Wu, Lauri Juvela\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: codec_vae\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We apply oversampling and anti-derivative anti-aliasing to the activation function to obtain its anti-aliased form, which eliminates \"folded-back\" aliasing artifacts while maintaining numerical stability and bounded gradients.\n  2. We replace the problematic ConvTranspose upsampling layer with a resampling approach combined with a noise-like high-pass filtered deterministic prior to avoid \"tonal artifacts\" and eliminate \"mirrored\" aliasing artifacts.\n  3. We introduce Pupu-Vocoder and Pupu-Codec, lightweight neural audio synthesis models built upon the proposed anti-aliased modules, and release high-quality pre-trained checkpoints to facilitate future research.\n  4. We construct a test signal benchmark to objectively demonstrate the effectiveness of the anti-aliased modules in suppressing aliasing artifacts.\n  5. We experimentally validate that the proposed models consistently outperform existing systems on singing voice, music, and audio synthesis while achieving comparable performance on speech.\n\nTags: Vocoder, 压缩", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "a8e80990-9f75-43e6-bbad-9b93e69ee810", "uuid": "6610606c-e3e8-4d28-a175-5cb171bfe896", "timestamp": "2026-08-13T08:45:06.487Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# Aliasing-Free Neural Audio Synthesis\narXiv: 2512.20211\nAuthors: Yicheng Gu, Junan Zhang, Chaoren Wang, Jerry Li, Zhizheng Wu, Lauri Juvela\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: codec_vae\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We apply oversampling and anti-derivative anti-aliasing to the activation function to obtain its anti-aliased form, which eliminates \"folded-back\" aliasing artifacts while maintaining numerical stability and bounded gradients.\n  2. We replace the problematic ConvTranspose upsampling layer with a resampling approach combined with a noise-like high-pass filtered deterministic prior to avoid \"tonal artifacts\" and eliminate \"mirrored\" aliasing artifacts.\n  3. We introduce Pupu-Vocoder and Pupu-Codec, lightweight neural audio synthesis models built upon the proposed anti-aliased modules, and release high-quality pre-trained checkpoints to facilitate future research.\n  4. We construct a test signal benchmark to objectively demonstrate the effectiveness of the anti-aliased modules in suppressing aliasing artifacts.\n  5. We experimentally validate that the proposed models consistently outperform existing systems on singing voice, music, and audio synthesis while achieving comparable performance on speech.\n\nTags: Vocoder, 压缩", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-84afd58cc43e92de", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# Vevo2: A Unified and Controllable Framework for Speech and Singing Voice Generation\narXiv: 2508.16332\nAuthors: Xueyao Zhang, Junan Zhang, Yuancheng Wang, Chaoren Wang, Yuanzhe Chen, Dongya Jia, Zhuo Chen, Zhizheng Wu\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We propose two audio tokenizers: a unified music-notation-free prosody tokenizer capable of encoding prosody and melody from speech, singing voice, and even instrumental sounds, and a unified timbre-disentangled content-style tokenizer that models linguistic content, prosody, and style for both speech and singing voice.\n  2. We introduce Vevo2, a unified and controllable framework for both speech and singing voice generation that applies versatile voice synthesis, conversion, and editing tasks by flexibly combining text, prosodic source, and style and timbre references during inference.\n  3. We propose a multi-objective post-training task for controllable voice generation that optimizes both intelligibility and prosody similarity rewards with a GRPO-based algorithm to achieve greater stability and improved overall performance.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-NAR-Flow, TTS/控制-参考语音, TTS/控制-风格标签, TTS/功能-RL优化, TTS/功能-多说话人", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "a8e80990-9f75-43e6-bbad-9b93e69ee810", "uuid": "2754b17e-b1ca-483d-a94c-cede446f4a62", "timestamp": "2026-08-13T08:45:06.771Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# Vevo2: A Unified and Controllable Framework for Speech and Singing Voice Generation\narXiv: 2508.16332\nAuthors: Xueyao Zhang, Junan Zhang, Yuancheng Wang, Chaoren Wang, Yuanzhe Chen, Dongya Jia, Zhuo Chen, Zhizheng Wu\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We propose two audio tokenizers: a unified music-notation-free prosody tokenizer capable of encoding prosody and melody from speech, singing voice, and even instrumental sounds, and a unified timbre-disentangled content-style tokenizer that models linguistic content, prosody, and style for both speech and singing voice.\n  2. We introduce Vevo2, a unified and controllable framework for both speech and singing voice generation that applies versatile voice synthesis, conversion, and editing tasks by flexibly combining text, prosodic source, and style and timbre references during inference.\n  3. We propose a multi-objective post-training task for controllable voice generation that optimizes both intelligibility and prosody similarity rewards with a GRPO-based algorithm to achieve greater stability and improved overall performance.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-NAR-Flow, TTS/控制-参考语音, TTS/控制-风格标签, TTS/功能-RL优化, TTS/功能-多说话人", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
