{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-95bc40a0d6bff083", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# GLM-4-Voice: Towards Intelligent and Human-Like End-to-End Spoken Chatbot\narXiv: 2412.02612\nAuthors: Aohan Zeng, Zhengxiao Du, Mingdao Liu, Kedong Wang, Shengmin Jiang, Lei Zhao, Yuxiao Dong, Jie Tang\nYear: 2024 | Venue: \nTopic: audio_understanding\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Introduction of an ultra-low bitrate (175bps), single-codebook speech tokenizer with 12.5Hz frame rate derived from an ASR model by incorporating a vector-quantized bottleneck into the encoder.\n  2. Synthesis of speech-text interleaved data from existing text pre-training corpora using a text-to-token model to efficiently transfer knowledge from text to speech modalities.\n  3. Continuation of pre-training from the GLM-4-9B text language model on a combination of unsupervised speech, interleaved speech-text, and supervised speech-text data, scaling up to 1 trillion tokens to achieve state-of-the-art performance in speech language modeling and spoken question answering.\n  4. Fine-tuning of the pre-trained model with high-quality conversational speech data using a \"streaming thoughts\" template to generate seamless, low-latency, and human-like spoken responses with controllable vocal nuances.\n  5. Demonstration of superior performance compared to existing spoken chatbot baselines in both conversational ability and speech quality while supporting bilingual Chinese and English interactions.\n\nTags: LALM, 压缩, TTS, LALM/对话型, LALM/音频标记-融合, 压缩/量化-VQ, 压缩/监督-有监督, 压缩/语义声学-语义, TTS/功能-流式", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "a8e80990-9f75-43e6-bbad-9b93e69ee810", "uuid": "3ebb2653-0792-4f9d-97f1-7a4b04aa50aa", "timestamp": "2026-08-13T08:45:26.531Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# GLM-4-Voice: Towards Intelligent and Human-Like End-to-End Spoken Chatbot\narXiv: 2412.02612\nAuthors: Aohan Zeng, Zhengxiao Du, Mingdao Liu, Kedong Wang, Shengmin Jiang, Lei Zhao, Yuxiao Dong, Jie Tang\nYear: 2024 | Venue: \nTopic: audio_understanding\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Introduction of an ultra-low bitrate (175bps), single-codebook speech tokenizer with 12.5Hz frame rate derived from an ASR model by incorporating a vector-quantized bottleneck into the encoder.\n  2. Synthesis of speech-text interleaved data from existing text pre-training corpora using a text-to-token model to efficiently transfer knowledge from text to speech modalities.\n  3. Continuation of pre-training from the GLM-4-9B text language model on a combination of unsupervised speech, interleaved speech-text, and supervised speech-text data, scaling up to 1 trillion tokens to achieve state-of-the-art performance in speech language modeling and spoken question answering.\n  4. Fine-tuning of the pre-trained model with high-quality conversational speech data using a \"streaming thoughts\" template to generate seamless, low-latency, and human-like spoken responses with controllable vocal nuances.\n  5. Demonstration of superior performance compared to existing spoken chatbot baselines in both conversational ability and speech quality while supporting bilingual Chinese and English interactions.\n\nTags: LALM, 压缩, TTS, LALM/对话型, LALM/音频标记-融合, 压缩/量化-VQ, 压缩/监督-有监督, 压缩/语义声学-语义, TTS/功能-流式", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
